{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.745104Z","id":"9bab01321405af8ab4a5e8a9d9d4b0fdc7679af7c60714b3c017cf47098ebb8c","body":{"detail":"Seen once on 2026-10-13 in a full vitest run of plugins/pi while a cargo build ran beside it (expect.poll(() => polls.length).toBe(1) received 7 within its 10 s). Alone, and in the next two full runs, it passed. trackPolls counts every DaemonClient's inject polls, so a poll of another loop, or a quick series of early returns paced by injectRetryMs (250 ms), would both count; which one this was is not known. Compare 6fab3d3d, a count flake in another tier 5 test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1148},"end":{"line":1181},"content_hash":"f569dab282bd8b4473edd666b40890f77340398bd460c8470e07f8ecb45763df"},"summary":"Unexplained flake: 'the injection loop never starts a stopped daemon, and resumes when one is back' saw 7 inject polls where it waits for 1","tags":["tests","flaky","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
